**Why the ChatGPT bridge is dead — two separate causes, both verified:**

1. 🔴 **Prompt-queue is switched OFF in Edge Profile 2 since 12:38:12 today.** Edge records it as a *user action* (`disable_reasons [1]`). At 12:35 the userscript session asked you to switch off **TTS Reader** and *leave Prompt-queue on*. Prompt-queue went off 2½ minutes later, and TTS Reader is still on. So most likely the wrong toggle was hit — nothing you need to explain. With the extension off, nothing runs, the native host dies silently, and the bridge sees "no live browser".
2. 🔴 **Even when it is switched back on, jobs will still fail** because of the September ChatGPT redesign. Prompt-queue's own hard-coded selectors are out of date:
   - A **new chat** fails at "Composer did not become ready" (the new lazy composer). That is the Sep-21 error.
   - **Reply capture** finds nothing on the new page, so the bridge never gets an answer.
   - The driftwatch pack itself is fine on the new page (11/16 ok, 0 broken). Prompt-queue just doesn't use it for those two steps.

